{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>And it shall be.</b> All people will be equal in this evil, and when two are paired like a kaf, it is a concise way. Likewise \"the master like the servant, and the servant like his master.\"" "<b>Like the lender.</b> He is the one who gives of his own [money] for free." "<b>Like the creditor.</b> He is the owner of the money." "<b>And he who bears [a debt].</b> He is the one who takes money against his pledge."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:54:54.008723520Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}